  "body": "I'm working on a project that includes building a simple custom video player using the `<video>` element and I noticed that the `readyState` property of `HTMLMediaElement` doesn't have a corresponding event to indicate when it has changed.\r\n\r\nIt seems possible to check `readyState` from the `progress` event that is fired for media download progress updates, but it isn't clear whether or not this will be 100% reliable.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me that a specific event for `readystatechange` would be helpful and simplify code that just needs to respond to changes in that state.",
